<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palancia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Palància</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palancia is a river of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> that rises in the Sierra de El Toro and flows south-east to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagunto">Sagunto</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>. The ancient Iberian and Roman town of Saguntum stood on a long hill above its lower course. Its valley carries the main route from Valencia towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teruel">Teruel</a> and Aragon.</p></div>
